"[2211.07691] Low-depth arithmetic circuit lower bounds via shifted partials (https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.07691)\nciteturn1view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.07691\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 160\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computational Complexity\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 14 Nov 2022]\nL9: # Title:Low-depth arithmetic circuit lower bounds via shifted partials\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Prashanth Amireddy , cite6†Ankit Garg , cite7†Neeraj Kayal , cite8†Chandan Saha , cite9†Bhargav Thankey L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Low-depth arithmetic circuit lower bounds via shifted partials, by Prashanth Amireddy and 4 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite10†View PDF cite11†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:We prove super-polynomial lower bounds for low-depth arithmetic circuits using the shifted partials measure [Gupta-Kamath-Kayal-Saptharishi, CCC 2013], [Kayal, ECCC 2012] and the affine projections of partials measure [Garg-Kayal-Saha, FOCS 2020], [Kayal-Nair-Saha, STACS 2016]. The recent breakthrough work of Limaye, Srinivasan and Tavenas [FOCS 2021] proved these lower bounds by proving lower bounds for low-depth set-multilinear circuits.\nL17: An interesting aspect of our proof is that it does not require conversion of a circuit to a set-multilinear circuit, nor does it involve a random restriction. We are able to upper bound the measures for homogeneous formulas directly, without going via set-multilinearity. Our lower bounds hold for the iterated matrix multiplication as well as the Nisan-Wigderson design polynomials.\nL18: We also define a subclass of homogeneous formulas which we call unique parse tree (UPT) formulas, and prove superpolynomial lower bounds for these. This generalizes the superpolynomial lower bounds for regular formulas in [Kayal-Saha-Saptharishi, STOC 2014], [Fournier-Limaye-Malod-Srinivasan, STOC 2014].\nL19: Subjects:  | Computational Complexity (cs.CC); Symbolic Computation (cs.SC)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite12†arXiv:2211.07691 [cs.CC]\nL21:    | (or cite13†arXiv:2211.07691v1 [cs.CC] for this version)\nL22:    | cite14†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2211.07691†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Prashanth Amireddy [cite15†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Mon, 14 Nov 2022 19:08:22 UTC (97 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled Low-depth arithmetic circuit lower bounds via shifted partials, by Prashanth Amireddy and 4 other authors\nL33: \nL34:   * cite10†View PDF L35:   * cite11†HTML (experimental) L36:   * cite16†TeX Source L37: \nL38: cite17†view license†creativecommons.org L39: ### Current browse context:\nL40: \nL41: cs.CC\nL42: \nL43: cite18†< prev |   cite19†next > L44: \nL45: cite20†new | cite21†recent | cite22†2022-11 L46: \nL47: Change to browse by:\nL48: \nL49: cite23†cs L50: cite24†cs.SC L51: \nL52: ### References & Citations\nL53: \nL54:   * cite25†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L55:   * cite26†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L56:   * cite27†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L57: \nL58: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL59: \nL60: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL61: \nL62: [Button: ×]\nL63: \nL64: loading...\nL65: \nL66: Data provided by:\nL67: \nL68: ### Bookmark\nL69: \nL70: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL71: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL72: \nL73: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL74: \nL75: Bibliographic Explorer (cite28†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL76: \nL77: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL78: \nL79: Connected Papers (cite2