/LIPIcs.CCC.2024.31`\nL86:   * cite75†Export XML L87:   * cite76†Export ACM-XML L88:   * cite77†Export DOAJ-XML L89:   * cite78†Export Schema.org L90:   * cite79†Export BibTeX L91: \nL92: * * *\nL93: # Low-Depth Algebraic Circuit Lower Bounds over Any Field\nL94: \nL95: ### Author cite80†Michael A. Forbes L96: \nL97: * * *\nL98: \nL99:   * Part of: Volume: cite81†39th Computational Complexity Conference (CCC 2024) L100: Part of: Series: cite6†Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs) L101: Part of: Conference: cite22†Computational Complexity Conference (CCC) L102:   * License:   cite82†Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license†creativecommons.org L103:   * Publication Date: 2024-07-15\nL104: \nL105: * * *\nL106: \nL107: cite83†PDF L108: ## File\nL109: \nL110: cite83†PDF LIPIcs.CCC.2024.31.pdf L111: \nL112:   * Filesize: 0.74 MB\nL113:   * 16 pages\nL114: \nL115: ## Document Identifiers\nL116: \nL117:   * DOI: cite84†10.4230/LIPIcs.CCC.2024.31†doi.org L118:   * URN: cite85†urn:nbn:de:0030-drops-204271†nbn-resolving.org L119: \nL120: ## Subject Classification\nL121: \nL122: ##### ACM Subject Classification\nL123: \nL124:   * Theory of computation → Algebraic complexity theory\nL125: \nL126: ##### Keywords\nL127: \nL128:   * algebraic circuits\nL129:   * lower bounds\nL130:   * low-depth circuits\nL131:   * positive characteristic\nL132: ## Metrics\nL133: \nL134:   * cite0†Access Statistics L135:   * Total Accesses (updated on a weekly basis)\nL136: \nL137: 0\nL138: \nL139: Document\nL140: \nL141: 0\nL142: \nL143: Metadata\nL144: \nL145: ##\nL146: ## Abstract\nL147:     The recent breakthrough of Limaye, Srinivasan and Tavenas [Limaye et al., 2022] (LST) gave the first super-polynomial lower bounds against low-depth algebraic circuits, for any field of zero (or sufficiently large) characteristic. It was an open question to extend this result to small-characteristic ([Limaye et al., 2022; Govindasamy et al., 2022; Fournier et al., 2023]), which in particular is relevant for an approach to prove superpolynomial AC⁰[p]-Frege lower bounds ([Govindasamy et al., 2022]).\nL148:     In this work, we prove super-polynomial algebraic circuit lower bounds against low-depth algebraic circuits over any field, with the same parameters as LST (or even matching the improved parameters of Bhargav, Dutta, and Saxena [Bhargav et al., 2022]). We give two proofs.\nL149: The first is logical, showing that even though the proof of LST naively fails in small characteristic, the proof is sufficiently algebraic that generic transfer results imply the result over characteristic zero implies the result over all fields. Motivated by this indirect proof, we then proceed to give a second constructive proof, replacing the field-dependent set-multilinearization result of LST with a set-multilinearization that works over any field, by using the Binet-Minc identity [Minc, 1979].\nL150: ## Cite As Get BibTex\nL151: \nL152: Michael A. Forbes. Low-Depth Algebraic Circuit Lower Bounds over Any Field. In 39th Computational Complexity Conference (CCC 2024). Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs), Volume 300, pp. 31:1-31:16, Schloss Dagstuhl – Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik (2024) cite84†https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.CCC.2024.31†doi.org L153: ##### BibTex\nL154: \nL155:     @InProceedings{forbes:LIPIcs.CCC.2024.31,\nL156:       author =\t{Forbes, Michael A.},\nL157:       title =\t{{Low-Depth Algebraic Circuit Lower Bounds over Any Field}},\nL158:       booktitle =\t{39th Computational Complexity Conference (CCC 2024)},\nL159:       pages =\t{31:1--31:16},\nL160:       series =\t{Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs)},\nL161:       ISBN =\t{978-3-95977-331-7},\nL162:       ISSN =\t{1868-8969},\nL163:       year =\t{2024},\nL164:       volume =\t{300},\nL165:       editor =\t{Santhanam, Rahul},\nL166:       publisher =\t{Schloss Dagstuhl -- Leibniz-Zentrum 